1110111011111100000000000000000000000000":2,"110011100011111110111011111100000000000000110011110100":2,"110011100011111110111011111100011110000111000000000000":2,"110011100011111110111011111100011110000111110011110100":2,"110011100011111110111011111100100000001000000100001011":2,"110011100011111110111011111100111110001111000100001011":1,"110011100011111110111011111100111110001111110111111111":2,"110011100011111110111111111111000001110000111011110100":1,"110011100011111110111111111111011111110111001000000000":1,"110011100011111110111111111111011111110111111011110100":1,"110011100011111110111111111111100001111000001100001011":1,"110011100011111110111111111111111111111111001100001011":2,"110011100011111110111111111111111111111111111111111111":1,"111111011111000001100000000000000000000000000000000000":1,"111111011111000001100000000000000000000000110011110100":1,"111111011111000001100000000000011110000111000000000000":1,"111111011111000001100000000000100000001000000100001011":2,"111111011111000001100000000000111110001111110111111111":2,"111111011111000001100100000011000001110000001000000000":2,"111111011111000001100100000011011111110111001000000000":1,"111111011111000001100100000011011111110111111011110100":1,"111111011111000001100100000011100001111000001100001011":3,"111111011111000001100100000011100001111000111111111111":1,"111111011111000001100100000011111111111111001100001011":1,"111111011111001111100011110000000000000000110011110100":1,"111111011111001111100011110000011110000111000000000000":1,"111111011111001111100011110000011110000111110011110100":1,"111111011111001111100011110000100000001000000100001011":1,"111111011111001111100011110000100000001000110111111111":1,"111111011111001111100111110011000001110000001000000000":1,"111111011111001111100111110011000001110000111011110100":1,"111111011111001111100111110011011111110111001000000000":1,"111111011111001111100111110011011111110111111011110100":1,"111111011111001111100111110011100001111000001100001011":3,"111111011111001111100111110011111111111111001100001011":1,"111111111111110001111000001100000000000000000000000000":2,"111111111111110001111000001100000000000000110011110100":2,"111111111111110001111000001100100000001000110111111111":2,"111111111111110001111000001100111110001111000100001011":2,"111111111111110001111100001111000001110000001000000000":1,"111111111111110001111100001111011111110111001000000000":2,"111111111111110001111100001111011111110111111011110100":1,"111111111111110001111100001111100001111000001100001011":2,"111111111111111111111011111100000000000000000000000000":1,"111111111111111111111011111100000000000000110011110100":2,"111111111111111111111011111100011110000111000000000000":3,"111111111111111111111011111100011110000111110011110100":1,"111111111111111111111011111100100000001000110111111111":1,"111111111111111111111011111100111110001111110111111111":2,"111111111111111111111111111111000001110000111011110100":2,"111111111111111111111111111111011111110111001000000000":1,"111111111111111111111111111111011111110111111011110100":2,"111111111111111111111111111111100001111000111111111111":1,"111111111111111111111111111111111111111111001100001011":1,"111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111":1}],"answer":"What I ran: I sent one job with 4 circuits to IQM's free Emerald test device, emerald:mock. Each circuit ran 250 shots. The job ID is 01a16483-c4ed-74f3-8193-ff08aa184200. It completed and cost 0 credits. The API reported 1.0 billed second, but mock jobs are free.\n\nHow I built it: Each circuit is the kicked Ising model on all 54 qubits of emerald. I used the 83 CZ couplers that the real emerald lists right now. One step applies RX(theta) to every qubit and then exp(i pi/4 ZZ) to every coupler. Each exp(i pi/4 ZZ) is exactly one CZ gate plus Z rotations on its two qubits. I folded those Z rotations into the phase of the next X rotation, so no extra gates were needed. I wrote the circuits directly in IQM's native gate format, so no compiler could add, merge, or remove a gate. I read the job back from the server. Each circuit has 249 CZ gates (83 couplers times 3 steps) and measures QB1 through QB54.\n\nResults, as magnetization (the average of Z over all 54 qubits, where +1 means every spin points up):\n- theta = 0: ideal 1.000, measured -0.004\n- theta = 0.2 pi: ideal 0.446, measured -0.014\n- theta = 0.35 pi: ideal 0.102, measured 0.016\n- theta = 0.5 pi: ideal 0.000, measured 0.013\n\nWhat a perfect quantum computer would show: With no sideways field (theta = 0), the spins never flip, so the magnetization stays at 1. As the field gets stronger, the field tips the spins and the couplings mix them, so the magnetization falls. It drops to about 0.45 at 0.2 pi, to about 0.10 at 0.35 pi, and to exactly 0 at 0.5 pi. That is the melting you asked about. A stronger sideways field destroys the up-pointing order faster. I computed these ideal values with an exact noise-free simulation. Each qubit's result depends only on qubits within 2 couplers of it, so a small exact simulation per qubit gives the exact 54-qubit answer. I checked that a larger region gives the same number.\n\nWhat the test device shows: The measured values are all near 0 and do not follow the ideal curve. That is expected. The mock device does not run the physics. It returns random bitstrings that do not depend on the circuit. The mock run proves that the job format, the 54-qubit layout, and the gate counts are right. To see the real melting curve with real noise, the same job would need to run on the real emerald, which costs credits. I did not do that because you asked for the free test device.\n\nFiles in the worktree: build_kim.py (builds the circuits and the ideal values), submit_kim.py, analyze_kim.py, kim_circuits.json, kim_ideals.json, kim_result.json, and job_log.txt. The counts field is empty on purpose because this job has 4 circuits. The counts for each circuit are in counts_list, in circuit order."}
